  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">GH: Many Hands Make Light Work: Eliminate slavery in child domestic work</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Impact: Children involved in child domestic work are free from abuse and exploitation and have their rights respected, enabling them to lead full and independent lives.

Main activities include: Income-generating activities (IGA) for vulnerable families, awareness raising for guardians, training of employers, psychosocial and legal support to abused Child Domestic Workers (CDWs) etc.

ASI has two sub-partners in Ghana: Challing Heights and Leadership &amp; Advocacy for Women in Africa (LAWA).</narrative>
  </description>
